$\alpha\to0$ limit $F^{*}_{0}=10$.  This is the $F\approx 2$–$2.5\times10$
inflation of the $F>10$ rule that is usually quoted as $F\approx23$ one
sided, $F\approx26$ two sided, essentially the Stock–Yogo $10\%$ maximal
relative bias $5\%$ size calibration $F_{SY}\approx16.4$ in the known
$\mu^{2}$ limit. ∎

